<p>The U.S. Senate on Wednesday rejected a Democratic-led effort to limit President Donald Trump&#x27;s military campaign against Iran, voting 52-47 against advancing the war powers resolution. It was the fourth failed attempt since the conflict began. The measure aimed to halt hostilities unless Congress specifically authorized them, underscoring a continuing constitutional fight over how much war authority a president can exercise without fresh approval from lawmakers. The vote showed that most senators support the administration&#x27;s current approach, with almost all Republicans opposing the resolution. For now, the result leaves Trump with political backing in the Senate even as the next phase of the conflict remains uncertain.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/eY3EwsfajDDuMIM4VZH6Fk279THmxXr61938-1x4Hyp2efNT4d1FPU-M3DQuyR02OlbDZJi_PWkrTqwL0cNZSKVed0h-XFpVPzHZ4BUqsIGjS_us0AaaEYMreEAbh0jfvzziyhsnuQj6v8VEQRbA3tY_6IZROZl6IgnoqhZo95DSHt1AGwJh_Yb5nMkugpGCLBXwbV_YTRskqh5RyMJM1WHZJhF1GAY4JHBHt4kjNhgrmah2CEiNR1RhCKhcqKJsai9BeQ' alt='U.S. Senate scene accompanying coverage of the vote on Iran war powers.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>GOP crossover remained rare: The Hindu reported that similar war powers votes since the conflict began have failed, with every Republican except Senator Rand Paul of Kentucky opposing them.</li><li>A wider conflict looms in the background: The Senate vote came as the U.S. and Iran were described as being in indirect talks to extend a two-week ceasefire, even as the war&#x27;s next phase remained uncertain.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Senate Democrats: Democrats framed the resolution as a defense of Congress&#x27;s war-making authority, arguing that U.S. forces should not stay involved in Iran-related hostilities without explicit approval from lawmakers. (<a href='https://www.reuters.com/world/us/us-senate-republicans-block-bid-rein-trump-iran-war-powers-voting-continues-2026-04-15/'>Reuters</a>)</li><li>Senate Republicans: Republicans used a procedural vote to keep the resolution from reaching the floor, showing little appetite within the party to rein in Trump during the conflict. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/us-senate-republicans-block-bid-rein-trump-iran-war-powers-voting-continues'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>President Trump: In his Sky News interview, Trump also criticized Keir Starmer&#x27;s energy and immigration policies, linking the Iran dispute to broader tensions with Britain. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/apr/15/iran-war-live-news-us-naval-blockade-strait-of-hormuz-pakistan-peace-talks-middle-east-crisis-latest'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/apr/15/iran-war-live-news-us-naval-blockade-strait-of-hormuz-pakistan-peace-talks-middle-east-crisis-latest'>US Senate fails to pass war powers resolution for fourth time – as it happened</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/us-senate-republicans-block-latest-bid-to-rein-in-trump-iran-war-powers2'>Senate Republicans block latest bid to rein in Trump Iran war powers</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/us-senate-republicans-block-latest-bid-to-rein-in-trump-iran-war-powers'>US Senate Republicans block latest bid to rein in Trump’s Iran war powers</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/us-senate-republicans-block-bid-rein-trump-iran-war-powers-voting-continues'>US Senate Republicans block bid to rein in Trump Iran war powers, voting continues</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/video/041526-the-takeout-with-major-garrett/'>4/15: The Takeout with Major Garrett</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-senate-republicans-block-latest-bid-to-rein-in-trump-iran-war-powers/article70866592.ece'>U.S. Senate Republicans b